{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he took his two wives and his two maidservants</b> — There is no earlier and later [chronological sequence] in this verse regarding the saving [i.e., the crossing to safety]. Rather, it says that he gathered his wives and his maidservants and his children to the bank of the stream, and he crossed alone to the ford of Jabbok to see whether the waters were high, and he returned and took them all with him as one and brought them across the stream, and afterward: <b>and he caused all that was his to pass over</b> — his livestock and his possessions."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:37.161378811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}